    "blocked_pending_decision": {
      "run_final_workflow_resume.py": "recovery_boundary.  Beyond the sha256 manifest it verifies a large file's identity as (st_size, st_mtime_ns).  BoundedRunContract.protected_manifest is Mapping[str, str] and verify_protected_manifest compares sha256 only, so the contract cannot express 'protect this large artifact by identity rather than by hashing it'.  That tradeoff is deliberate in the driver (hashing a very large file is expensive), and it is common runner semantics rather than a quirk, so it needs a design decision: a second protected_identity mapping, or mandate sha256, or declare it the caller's job."
    },
